  "body": "Visitors could lose the entire login page when browser storage was denied, and the backend advertised HTTP 200 readiness while it could not serve requests. This increment keeps optional preferences in memory, treats inaccessible session caches as absent, and returns 503/Retry-After with valid Spanish UTF-8 until initialization completes.\n\nValidation before integrating current main: 210 UI suites / 2,005 tests; final browser regression 38 passed / 4 explicit skips across desktop/phone/tablet Chromium and critical Firefox/WebKit, with axe checks after settled fonts/animations. Both new storage-denial cases failed before the repair. Production UI build passed at 357,222 gzip bytes initial JS. Two Hspec startup-response cases passed. Existing pinned TLC/Alloy event and social runners passed their positive models and expected negative controls. Full hosted gates remain required on this head after the main merge.\n\nThe audit inventory, role-policy matrix, confirmed findings, limitations, commands, screenshots and rollout checkpoint are in `docs/ux-ui-audit/2026-09-17/README.md`. This is a partial delivery, not completion of the full UX/UI audit. Authentication/onboarding model-conformance, protected/native runtime coverage and broader ES/EN work remain open.\n\nNo migration, role/flag change or mobile-pointer update. Mobile recovery is tracked in https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/89; promoting its current main requires resolving the existing artist-activation API dependency. Production mutation is paused because the operator confirmed another deployment in progress. Rollback: revert the browser change if needed; preserve accurate 503 readiness/UTF-8 when recovering the service rather than restoring false health. No task deployment or store publication is claimed.\n",
